"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[12628],{612628:e=>{e.exports="# Visual Type Mappings\n\nStructured mapping from Tableau visual types (mark types) to Lakeview widget types.\n\n## Quick Reference Table\n\n| Tableau Mark Type               | Lakeview Widget  | Version | Status                |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------- | ------- | --------------------- |\n| `Bar`                           | `bar`            | 3       | ✅ Supported          |\n| `Line`                          | `line`           | 3       | ✅ Supported          |\n| `Area`                          | `area`           | 3       | ✅ Supported          |\n| `Circle`                        | `scatter`        | 3       | ✅ Supported          |\n| `Square`                        | `heatmap`        | 3       | ✅ Supported          |\n| `Shape`                         | `scatter`        | 3       | ✅ Supported          |\n| `Text`                          | `table`          | 1       | ✅ Supported          |\n| `Pie`                           | `pie`            | 3       | ✅ Supported          |\n| `Map` / `Filled Map`            | `choropleth-map` | 3       | ✅ Supported          |\n| `Polygon`                       | `choropleth-map` | 3       | ✅ Supported          |\n| Symbol Map (Circle on Lat/Long) | `symbol-map`     | 2       | ✅ Supported          |\n| `Gantt Bar`                     | -                | -       | ❌ Not Supported      |\n| `Density`                       | -                | -       | ❌ Not Supported      |\n| `Box`                           | `box`            | 3       | ✅ Supported          |\n| `Automatic`                     | Varies           | -       | ⚠️ Requires inference |\n\n## Visual Type Mappings (by Tableau Chart Type)\n\n| Tableau Visual             | Lakeview Widget  | Version | Status           | Notes                                  |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------- | ------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| Bar Chart (Vertical)       | `bar`            | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Dimension on Columns, Measure on Rows  |\n| Bar Chart (Horizontal)     | `bar`            | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Same mapping, orientation differs      |\n| Stacked Bar                | `bar`            | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Color encoding for stacking            |\n| Grouped Bar (Side-by-Side) | `bar`            | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Color encoding for grouping            |\n| Line Chart                 | `line`           | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Temporal x-axis recommended            |\n| Area Chart                 | `area`           | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Same as line, filled                   |\n| Stacked Area               | `area`           | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Color encoding for stacking            |\n| Pie Chart                  | `pie`            | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Angle for measure, Color for dimension |\n| Donut Chart                | `pie`            | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Same as pie (Lakeview handles styling) |\n| Scatter Plot               | `scatter`        | 3       | ✅ Supported     | X and Y both quantitative              |\n| Bubble Chart               | `scatter`        | 3       | ⚠️ Partial       | Size encoding limited                  |\n| Text Table                 | `table`          | 1       | ✅ Supported     | STRICT schema - 21 properties required |\n| Crosstab                   | `pivot`          | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Dimensions on both Rows AND Columns    |\n| Highlight Table            | `heatmap`        | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Color intensity by measure             |\n| Histogram                  | `histogram`      | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Binned dimension + count               |\n| Filled Map (Choropleth)    | `choropleth-map` | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Geographic dimension + color measure   |\n| Symbol Map                 | `symbol-map`     | 2       | ✅ Supported     | Lat/Long + size/color                  |\n| KPI / Big Number           | `counter`        | 2       | ✅ Supported     | Single aggregated value                |\n| Dual Axis Chart            | `combo`          | 1       | ⚠️ Partial       | May require separate widgets           |\n| Treemap                    | -                | -       | ❌ Not Supported | Use bar or pivot alternative           |\n| Box Plot                   | `box`            | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Category + value distribution          |\n| Gantt Chart                | -                | -       | ❌ Not Supported | No direct equivalent                   |\n| Bullet Graph               | -                | -       | ❌ Not Supported | Use bar as alternative                 |\n| Word Cloud                 | -                | -       | ❌ Not Supported | No direct equivalent                   |\n| Waterfall Chart            | `waterfall`      | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Categorical + cumulative values        |\n| Funnel Chart               | `funnel`         | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Stage + value                          |\n| Sankey Diagram             | `sankey`         | 1       | ✅ Supported     | Source + target + value                |\n| Forecast Line              | `forecast-line`  | 3       | ✅ Supported     | Line with forecast values              |\n| Text / Markdown            | `text`           | -       | ✅ Supported     | Non-data markdown content              |\n\n## Detailed Mapping Table\n\n```yaml\nmappings:\n  # Bar Charts\n  - tableau_mark: Bar\n    tableau_visual: 'Bar Chart'\n    lakeview: bar\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    shelf_mappings:\n      Columns: x\n      Rows: y\n      Color: color\n      Size: N/A # Bar width not adjustable\n      Label: frame.showDataLabels\n      Detail: query fields\n      Tooltip: tooltip\n    notes: |\n      Vertical bars: Dimension on Columns, Measure on Rows\n      Horizontal bars: Reverse (Lakeview always uses x for category)\n      Stacking controlled by color encoding presence\n\n  - tableau_mark: Bar\n    tableau_visual: 'Stacked Bar'\n    lakeview: bar\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    shelf_mappings:\n      Columns: x\n      Rows: y\n      Color: color # Creates stacking\n    notes: Color dimension creates stacked segments\n\n  - tableau_mark: Bar\n    tableau_visual: 'Grouped Bar (Side-by-Side)'\n    lakeview: bar\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    shelf_mappings:\n      Columns: x\n      Rows: y\n      Color: color # Creates grouping\n    notes: Same encoding as stacked; Lakeview rendering determines grouping\n\n  # Line Charts\n  - tableau_mark: Line\n    tableau_visual: 'Line Chart'\n    lakeview: line\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    shelf_mappings:\n      Columns: x # Typically temporal\n      Rows: y\n      Color: color # Multiple series\n      Path: N/A # Line connection order\n    notes: Use temporal scale for date x-axis\n\n  - tableau_mark: Line\n    tableau_visual: 'Dual-Line'\n    lakeview: line\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    notes: Multiple measures become separate y-fields or separate widgets\n\n  # Area Charts\n  - tableau_mark: Area\n    tableau_visual: 'Area Chart'\n    lakeview: area\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    shelf_mappings:\n      Columns: x\n      Rows: y\n      Color: color\n    notes: Same as line chart, filled\n\n  - tableau_mark: Area\n    tableau_visual: 'Stacked Area'\n    lakeview: area\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    notes: Color encoding creates stacked areas\n\n  # Pie Charts\n  - tableau_mark: Pie\n    tableau_visual: 'Pie Chart'\n    lakeview: pie\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    shelf_mappings:\n      Angle: angle # Measure determines slice size\n      Color: color # Dimension determines slices\n      Label: frame.showDataLabels\n    notes: Angle shelf maps to measure, Color shelf maps to dimension\n\n  - tableau_mark: Pie\n    tableau_visual: 'Donut Chart'\n    lakeview: pie\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    notes: Same as pie; Lakeview may not have explicit donut mode\n\n  # Scatter / Bubble Charts\n  - tableau_mark: Circle\n    tableau_visual: 'Scatter Plot'\n    lakeview: scatter\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    shelf_mappings:\n      Columns: x # Measure\n      Rows: y # Measure\n      Color: color\n      Size: size # Creates bubble effect\n      Detail: query fields # Increases point count\n    notes: Both axes quantitative for true scatter\n\n  - tableau_mark: Shape\n    tableau_visual: 'Scatter with Shapes'\n    lakeview: scatter\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    notes: Shape encoding not directly supported; maps to scatter\n\n  - tableau_mark: Circle\n    tableau_visual: 'Bubble Chart'\n    lakeview: scatter\n    version: 3\n    status: partial\n    shelf_mappings:\n      Columns: x\n      Rows: y\n      Size: size\n      Color: color\n    notes: Size encoding creates bubbles; verify Lakeview size support\n\n  # Tables\n  - tableau_mark: Text\n    tableau_visual: 'Text Table'\n    lakeview: table\n    version: 1\n    status: supported\n    shelf_mappings:\n      Rows: columns # Dimensions as row headers\n      Columns: N/A # Simple table has no column dimension\n      Text: values # Measures displayed\n    notes: |\n      CRITICAL: Table widget has STRICT schema with 21 required column properties\n      Set disaggregated based on fields: false if any MEASURE()/aggregation, true only for raw column refs\n\n  - tableau_mark: Text\n    tableau_visual: 'Crosstab'\n    lakeview: pivot\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    shelf_mappings:\n      Rows: rows\n      Columns: columns\n      Text: values\n    notes: |\n      Dimensions on BOTH Rows AND Columns → use pivot widget\n      Dimensions on Rows ONLY → use table widget\n\n  - tableau_mark: Square\n    tableau_visual: 'Highlight Table'\n    lakeview: heatmap\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    shelf_mappings:\n      Rows: y # Categorical\n      Columns: x # Categorical\n      Color: color # Intensity by measure\n    notes: Color intensity represents measure value\n\n  # Maps\n  - tableau_mark: Map\n    tableau_visual: 'Filled Map (Choropleth)'\n    lakeview: choropleth-map\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    shelf_mappings:\n      Detail: geo / location\n      Color: color\n    notes: |\n      Geographic dimension determines regions\n      Color measure determines fill intensity\n      Supported regions: countries, US states, limited others\n\n  - tableau_mark: Polygon\n    tableau_visual: 'Polygon Map'\n    lakeview: choropleth-map\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    notes: Same as filled map\n\n  - tableau_mark: Circle\n    tableau_visual: 'Symbol Map'\n    lakeview: symbol-map\n    version: 2\n    status: supported\n    shelf_mappings:\n      Columns: longitude # Maps to coordinates.longitude\n      Rows: latitude # Maps to coordinates.latitude\n      Size: size\n      Color: color\n    notes: |\n      Requires Lat/Long fields; Size creates proportional symbols.\n      Lakeview uses nested coordinates structure:\n      encodings:\n        coordinates:\n          latitude: {fieldName: \"lat_field\", displayName: \"Latitude\"}\n          longitude: {fieldName: \"lon_field\", displayName: \"Longitude\"}\n\n  # KPI / Counter\n  - tableau_mark: Text\n    tableau_visual: 'KPI / Big Number'\n    lakeview: counter\n    version: 2\n    status: supported\n    shelf_mappings:\n      Text: value # Single aggregated measure\n    notes: |\n      Single measure display\n      Use disaggregated: false with aggregation\n\n  # Other Supported\n  - tableau_mark: Bar\n    tableau_visual: 'Histogram'\n    lakeview: histogram\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    notes: Binned dimension on x-axis, count on y-axis\n\n  - tableau_mark: Bar\n    tableau_visual: 'Waterfall Chart'\n    lakeview: waterfall\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    notes: Sequential categorical values with running total\n\n  - tableau_mark: Bar\n    tableau_visual: 'Funnel Chart'\n    lakeview: funnel\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    shelf_mappings:\n      Category: y\n      Measure: x\n    notes: Stage dimension + value measure\n\n  - tableau_mark: N/A\n    tableau_visual: 'Sankey Diagram'\n    lakeview: sankey\n    version: 1\n    status: supported\n    notes: Source + target dimensions + value measure\n\n  # Box Plot\n  - tableau_mark: N/A\n    tableau_visual: 'Box Plot'\n    lakeview: box\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    shelf_mappings:\n      Category: category # Categorical dimension\n      Measure: value # Distribution values\n      Color: color # Optional grouping\n    notes: |\n      Shows distribution statistics: min, max, median, quartiles\n      Category dimension on x-axis, measure on y-axis\n\n  # Forecast Line\n  - tableau_mark: Line\n    tableau_visual: 'Line with Forecast'\n    lakeview: forecast-line\n    version: 3\n    status: supported\n    notes: |\n      Requires dataset with columns: value, value_forecast, value_forecast_lower, value_forecast_upper\n      Used for predictive analytics visualizations\n\n  # Text / Markdown\n  - tableau_mark: N/A\n    tableau_visual: 'Text Box / Caption'\n    lakeview: text\n    version: null # No version for text widget\n    status: supported\n    notes: |\n      Non-data widget for markdown content\n      No queries attached\n      Uses textbox_spec instead of spec\n\n  # Dual Axis / Combo\n  - tableau_mark: Mixed\n    tableau_visual: 'Dual Axis Chart'\n    lakeview: combo\n    version: 1\n    status: partial\n    notes: |\n      Use combo (version 1) for mixed bar+line, or standard bar/line/area with y.primary + y.secondary encoding for same-type dual axis.\n      Consider separate widgets if complex.\n\n  # Unsupported\n  - tableau_mark: Square\n    tableau_visual: 'Treemap'\n    lakeview: null\n    status: unsupported\n    alternatives:\n      - bar (single level)\n      - pivot (multi-level)\n      - heatmap (two dimensions)\n    notes: |\n      No treemap widget in Lakeview\n      Detail shelf → hierarchy\n      Size shelf → measure\n      Document as skipped, suggest alternative\n\n  - tableau_mark: 'Gantt Bar'\n    tableau_visual: 'Gantt Chart'\n    lakeview: null\n    status: unsupported\n    notes: No direct equivalent; consider timeline or bar chart\n\n  - tableau_mark: Density\n    tableau_visual: 'Density Mark'\n    lakeview: null\n    status: unsupported\n    notes: No density/heatmap-style mark in Lakeview\n\n  - tableau_mark: N/A\n    tableau_visual: 'Bullet Graph'\n    lakeview: null\n    status: unsupported\n    alternatives:\n      - bar with reference line\n    notes: No bullet graph widget; use bar chart as approximation\n\n  - tableau_mark: N/A\n    tableau_visual: 'Word Cloud'\n    lakeview: null\n    status: unsupported\n    notes: No text visualization widget\n\n  - tableau_mark: N/A\n    tableau_visual: 'Radial / Radar Chart'\n    lakeview: null\n    status: unsupported\n    notes: No radial chart widget\n```\n\n## Status Legend\n\n| Status        | Description                                  |\n| ------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `supported`   | Full mapping available, documented           |\n| `partial`     | Mapping exists but some features may be lost |\n| `unsupported` | No Lakeview equivalent                       |\n\n## Shelf to Encoding Mapping\n\n```yaml\nshelf_mappings:\n  # Position encodings\n  Columns:\n    chart_types: [bar, line, area, scatter, heatmap]\n    lakeview_encoding: x\n    scale_types:\n      dimension: categorical\n      date: temporal\n      measure: quantitative\n\n  Rows:\n    chart_types: [bar, line, area, scatter, heatmap]\n    lakeview_encoding: y\n    scale_types:\n      dimension: categorical\n      measure: quantitative\n\n  # Appearance encodings\n  Color:\n    lakeview_encoding: color\n    scale_types:\n      dimension: categorical\n      measure: quantitative # gradient\n\n  Size:\n    lakeview_encoding: size\n    supported_widgets: [scatter]\n    notes: Limited support; primarily for bubble charts\n\n  Shape:\n    lakeview_encoding: N/A\n    notes: Not directly supported; marks have fixed shapes\n\n  # Data encodings\n  Detail:\n    lakeview_encoding: query fields\n    notes: |\n      Adds fields to query for increased granularity\n      Does NOT add visual encoding\n\n  Label:\n    lakeview_encoding: frame.showDataLabels\n    notes: Boolean flag to show/hide data labels\n\n  Tooltip:\n    lakeview_encoding: tooltip fields\n    notes: Additional fields shown on hover\n\n  # Pie-specific\n  Angle:\n    lakeview_encoding: angle\n    notes: Measure that determines slice size\n\n  # Pivot-specific\n  Rows_dimension:\n    lakeview_encoding: rows\n    notes: For pivot widget only\n\n  Columns_dimension:\n    lakeview_encoding: columns\n    notes: For pivot widget only\n\n  Values:\n    lakeview_encoding: values\n    notes: For pivot widget only\n```\n\n## Mark Type Detection Rules\n\nWhen the worksheet's mark class is `Automatic`, you must infer the mark type from shelf contents in the XML. Read the worksheet's `<style>/<style-rule><format attr='mark-class'>` to find the explicit mark, otherwise apply the resolution below.\n\n**Tableau's official Automatic mark resolution** (source: help.tableau.com — \"Change the Type of Mark in the View\"):\n\nThe inner fields on the Rows and Columns shelves determine the mark type:\n\n| Inner Field Configuration           | Resolved Mark   | Lakeview Widget |\n| ----------------------------------- | --------------- | --------------- |\n| Date on one axis + Measure on other | Line            | line            |\n| Non-date Dimension + Measure        | Bar             | bar             |\n| Measures on both Rows AND Columns   | Shape (scatter) | scatter         |\n| Dimensions on both Rows AND Columns | Text (crosstab) | pivot or table  |\n\n**How to identify dates vs dimensions vs measures from the XML:**\n\n- **Dates**: The column instance carries a date derivation — values like `Month-Trunc`, `Year-Trunc`, `Quarter-Trunc`, `Week-Trunc`, `Day-Trunc`, `Hour-Trunc` (look for `derivation=` attributes on `<column-instance>` and date/time-related field names).\n- **Measures**: Aggregation derivations — `Sum`, `Avg`, `Count`, `CountD`, `Min`, `Max`, `Median`. Also: column has `role='measure'` or appears with an aggregation wrapper on the shelf.\n- **Dimensions**: No aggregation derivation (or `None`), or `role='dimension'`.\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Both continuous and discrete dates resolve to Line. The continuous/discrete distinction only affects axis rendering (smooth axis vs. individual ticks), NOT the chart type.\n\nAdditional inference rules for Automatic marks:\n\n| Shelf / Encoding Pattern                                          | Lakeview Widget |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------- |\n| Geographic dimension on Detail                                    | choropleth-map  |\n| Lat/Long on Columns/Rows                                          | symbol-map      |\n| Crosstab layout (dims on Rows + Columns) with measure on Color    | heatmap         |\n| Text/label mark with measures on the Text shelf and no dimensions | counter         |\n| Angle shelf has a measure                                         | pie             |\n\n## Migration Decision Tree\n\n```\nSTART: Identify Tableau Mark Type\n│\n├─ Mark Type = \"Bar\"\n│   └─ Widget: bar v3\n│       └─ Check if horizontal → swap x/y conceptually\n│\n├─ Mark Type = \"Line\"\n│   └─ Widget: line v3\n│       └─ Check if date on x → use temporal scale\n│\n├─ Mark Type = \"Area\"\n│   └─ Widget: area v3\n│\n├─ Mark Type = \"Circle\"\n│   ├─ Has Lat/Long on shelves?\n│   │   ├─ Yes → Widget: symbol-map v3\n│   │   └─ No → Widget: scatter v3\n│   └─ Has Size encoding?\n│       └─ Yes → Bubble chart (scatter with size)\n│\n├─ Mark Type = \"Square\"\n│   ├─ Has Detail shelf with hierarchy?\n│   │   ├─ Yes → Treemap (NOT SUPPORTED) → suggest alternatives\n│   │   └─ No → Widget: heatmap v3\n│\n├─ Mark Type = \"Text\"\n│   ├─ Dimensions on BOTH Rows AND Columns?\n│   │   ├─ Yes → Widget: pivot v3\n│   │   └─ No → Widget: table v1 (STRICT schema!)\n│   └─ Single aggregated value (KPI)?\n│       └─ Yes → Widget: counter v2\n│\n├─ Mark Type = \"Pie\"\n│   └─ Widget: pie v3\n│\n├─ Mark Type = \"Map\" or \"Polygon\"\n│   └─ Widget: choropleth-map v3\n│\n├─ Mark Type = \"Shape\"\n│   └─ Widget: scatter v3 (shape encoding not preserved)\n│\n├─ Mark Type = \"Gantt Bar\"\n│   └─ NOT SUPPORTED → document and skip\n│\n├─ Mark Type = \"Density\"\n│   └─ NOT SUPPORTED → document and skip\n│\n├─ Mark Type = \"Box\"\n│   └─ Widget: box v3\n│       └─ Category dimension + measure for distribution\n│\n└─ Mark Type = \"Automatic\"\n    └─ Infer from shelf configuration (see inference rules)\n```\n\n## Agent Quick-Reference: Chart Type Inference\n\nResolve the worksheet's mark + shelf layout from the XML, then pick a widget:\n\n| Resolved Mark / Layout                                          | Lakeview Widget                        | Version |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| mark = Bar                                                      | bar                                    | 3       |\n| mark = Line                                                     | line                                   | 3       |\n| mark = Area                                                     | area                                   | 3       |\n| mark = Pie                                                      | pie                                    | 3       |\n| mark = Circle / Shape (no Lat/Long)                             | scatter                                | 3       |\n| mark = Map / Polygon                                            | choropleth-map (v3) or symbol-map (v2) | -       |\n| mark = Text + crosstab layout + color encoding has measure      | **heatmap**                            | 3       |\n| mark = Text + single label measure (no dims on Rows/Columns)    | **counter**                            | 2       |\n| mark = Text + multiple label measures (no dims on Rows/Columns) | **multiple counter widgets**           | 2       |\n| mark = Text + dims on BOTH Rows AND Columns                     | **pivot**                              | 3       |\n| mark = Text + dims on Rows ONLY                                 | **table**                              | 1       |\n\n**Multi-KPI Special Case:**\nWhen the mark is Text, no dims sit on Rows/Columns, and the Text shelf has 2+ measures:\n\n- Create a separate counter widget for each measure\n- Divide width equally: `widget_width = floor(total_width / measure_count)`\n\n**Unsupported (create text placeholder):**\n\n- treemap, gantt, bullet, word cloud, density, radial\n\n---\n\n## Critical Migration Notes\n\n1. **Table Widget STRICT Schema:** The `table` widget (v1) requires ALL 21 column properties. Missing properties cause validation failures. See `lakeview/widgets/table.md`.\n\n2. **Table vs Pivot Decision:**\n   - Dimensions on Rows ONLY → `table` v1\n   - Dimensions on BOTH Rows AND Columns → `pivot` v3\n\n3. **Treemap Alternative Selection:**\n   - Single hierarchy level → `bar` chart\n   - Two dimensions → `heatmap`\n   - Multi-level with values → `pivot` table\n\n4. **Dual Axis Charts:** May require `combo` widget or separate widgets. Complex dual-axis configurations may not migrate directly.\n\n5. **Symbol vs Choropleth Maps:**\n   - Geographic dimension (State, Country) → `choropleth-map`\n   - Explicit Lat/Long fields → `symbol-map`\n\n6. **Aggregation Preservation:** Ensure the aggregation type (SUM, COUNT, AVG) from Tableau is preserved in the Lakeview query expression.\n\n7. **Date Handling:** Use `temporal` scale type for date dimensions on x-axis; `categorical` for non-date dimensions.\n\n8. **Color Encoding Behavior:** Color dimension creates:\n   - Stacked segments (bar/area)\n   - Multiple series (line)\n   - Grouped categories (scatter)\n"}}]);
